!.env.example

# Fetched datasets. Third-party data (CC-BY-4.0), ~24MB, and reproducible
# with `python -m eval_pipeline.mtbench` — so the fetch command is the
# artefact worth keeping, not the bytes.
data/*.jsonl

# The assessment prompt itself is the company's material — keep it out of a
# repo that will be pushed publicly.
*.pdf

# Cached judge responses — real verdicts, but paid for locally.
.judge_cache.jsonl
.reward_hacking_cache.jsonl
